      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T13:15:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Microdroid also uses the sample data [1].\n\n\u003e But - what does it mean for Rialto to support a non-protected VM? Such a VM shouldn\u0027t get any attestation certificate, should it?\n\nNon-protected rialto only runs in tests. When rialto is used as service VM. It is always protected [2]. Otherwise, the non-protected cannot get any certificate with the sample DICE chain as UDS is fake + it won\u0027t have the pvmfw maker in DICE chain, the RKP server will never issue a certificate.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid_manager/src/dice.rs;l\u003d61;drc\u003d95084dfd8587992bb384759544678fd0ab5cef8b\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/service_vm_manager/src/lib.rs;l\u003d198;drc\u003d19723cae2bdab3b06a0db0472640ba25b74a5a7d",
      "parentUuid": "43072069_77f0c7ce",
